{"name":"White Glove","hex":"#f0efed","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"white-glove","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Scrupulous, painstaking, meticulous."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white-glove"}],"entries":[{"title":"Glove","blocks":[{"text":"A glove is a garment covering the hand, with separate sheaths or openings for each finger including the thumb. Gloves protect and comfort hands against cold or heat, damage by friction, abrasion or chemicals, and disease; or in turn to provide a guard for what a bare hand should not touch."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Centre_de_Documentaci%C3%B3_Museu_T%C3%A8xtil_de_Terrassa-_Reserves-_Teixits-_Guants002.JPG/330px-Centre_de_Documentaci%C3%B3_Museu_T%C3%A8xtil_de_Terrassa-_Reserves-_Teixits-_Guants002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glove","wikidata":"Q169031"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White","wikidata":"Q23444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Centre_de_Documentaci%C3%B3_Museu_T%C3%A8xtil_de_Terrassa-_Reserves-_Teixits-_Guants002.JPG/500px-Centre_de_Documentaci%C3%B3_Museu_T%C3%A8xtil_de_Terrassa-_Reserves-_Teixits-_Guants002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&u